% ============================================================================
% compound-speleothem-surface.query.adj — worked recall over the DERIVED
% compound-speleothem-surface rule.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to answer "does a column touch
% the ceiling or the floor?" — a question `speleothem-growth-surface.adj`
% correctly REFUSED to answer, because `speleothem_growth_surface` means
% the surface a speleothem grows FROM and a column does not grow from a
% surface at all; it is two speleothems that met.
%
% The question was never unanswerable. It was not a question about growth
% surfaces. Here it is answered in a relation that means what the answer
% means — the surfaces reached by this speleothem's components — and the
% answer is BOTH, each traceable to a different source sentence.
%
% Two answers are correct in this relation where two rows would have been a
% misrepresentation in that one. That is the argument for abstaining rather
% than fudging, made concrete: because the table declined, the honest
% answer stayed available as a composition, in its own name, with its
% provenance intact.
%
% It states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the rule library (which
% imports both premise libraries) and asks binding queries.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative imports resolve):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli compound-speleothem-surface.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "compound-speleothem-surface.adj"

? compound_speleothem_surface(column, $S)      % expect cave_ceiling AND cave_floor -- DERIVED via the two components
? compound_speleothem_surface($C, cave_floor)  % expect column (reverse through the rule)
? compound_speleothem_surface(helictite, $S)   % expect abstain -- absent from BOTH premises; composition propagates abstention
? compound_speleothem_surface(stalactite, $S)  % expect abstain -- not a compound speleothem, so nothing to decompose
